mcs51 peephole: add operandOffset condition function

operandOffset('N' %1 %2) checks that two symbolic operands refer to the
same base symbol with addresses that differ by exactly N bytes, i.e.
%2 == %1 + N.  It recognizes sequential memory accesses in generated
code, such as 'mov dptr,#(_sym + 0x0001)' after 'mov dptr,#_sym', which
a rule can then rewrite into a cheaper increment.

For example, mcs51 rule 1012 collapses

  mov dptr,%1 / movx %3,%4 / mov dptr,%2   if operandOffset('1' %1 %2)

into

  mov dptr,%1 / movx %3,%4 / inc dptr

saving two bytes and one cycle per collapsed reload.

Implementation:
  - parseSymAddr decomposes an SDCC symbolic address of the forms
    "(_sym + 0xNN)", "_sym" or a plain numeric literal into a
    (symbol, offset) pair; a '#' immediate prefix is stripped first.
  - setFromConditionArgs builds its set LIFO (addSetHead), so the
    arguments arrive in reverse rule-text order; this is documented at
    the argument-collecting block.

Part of a series splitting a larger mcs51 peephole set into independent
pieces.

--- SDCCpeeph.c	2026-03-11 09:20:48.000000000 +0100
+++ SDCCpeeph.c	2026-03-12 17:00:00.000000000 +0100
